WEBVTT

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:03.575
At the very top of the system are three domains.

00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:09.249
Bacteria are single-celled prokaryotes, meaning their cells have no nucleus.

00:00:09.249 --> 00:00:13.162
They live almost everywhere, including inside your own body.

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:22.217
Archaea are also single-celled prokaryotes, but their chemistry is different enough from bacteria that they get their own domain.

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:26.557
Many live in extreme places, like hot springs and very salty water.

00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:33.292
Eukarya includes every organism whose cells have a nucleus and membrane-bound organelles.

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:37.357
That means you, along with every plant, fungus, and protist.

00:00:38.607 --> 00:00:41.958
The domain Eukarya is split into four kingdoms.

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:45.667
A useful way to compare them is how they get energy.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:49.802
Autotrophs make their own food, usually by photosynthesis.

00:00:49.802 --> 00:00:53.867
Heterotrophs have to get their food from other organisms.
